#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179426 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7abceeb-620d-5e95-93ca-30bc557cf007" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Vector Field From Its Stream Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a779f67a-21ee-5eb4-8355-c69476ee0d3e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12395" :question/problem "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $\\psi(x,y) = e^{x} \\cos{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "A function $\\psi(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $\\mathbf F= P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP = \\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial y},\\qquad Q = -\\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $\\psi(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $\\psi(x,y) = e^{x} \\cos{y}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc613be0-2d34-5253-8fbe-7d2a5fcd0840" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cases Where a Stream Function Exists"}] :question/id #uuid "69a293cc-ff8c-5485-8329-12e87e1addff" :question/math-academy-id "e-12396" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\n- $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = x^4y\\,\\mathbf{i} - 2x^3y^2\\,\\mathbf{j}$\n\n- $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = \\sin x \\sin y\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\cos x \\cos y\\,\\mathbf{j}$\n\n- $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = 4x^2y\\,\\mathbf{i} -4x^2y^2\\,\\mathbf{j}$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $\\mathbf{F} = P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ with a simply connected domain $D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2$ has a stream function $\\psi(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} = 0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4{x}^{3}y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-4{x}^{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\n= 4x^3y + (- 4x^3y)\n= 0\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\n= \\cos x \\sin y + (- \\cos x \\sin y)\n= 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=8xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-8{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\n= 8xy + (- 8x^2y)\n\\neq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179435 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30cae81-5bda-52dc-8de4-9ad5fd587e48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Streamlines of Vector Fields"}] :question/id #uuid "6cb53e89-c4a9-57a6-b54f-f6a09d3a17d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-12439" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the streamline that passes through the point $P(-1,1)$ for the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = (x^3-3xy^2)\\,\\mathbf{i} + (y^3-3x^2y)\\,\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $\\mathbf F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $\\mathbf{F} = P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ with a simply connected domain $D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2$ has a stream function $\\psi(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} = 0.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = (x^3-3xy^2)\\,\\mathbf{i} + (y^3-3x^2y)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D=\\mathbb{R}^2,$ where $P(x,y) = x^3-3xy^2$ and $Q(x,y) = y^3 - 3x^2y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =3{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\mathbf F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} = (3x^2-3y^2) + (3y^2 - 3x^2) = 0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $\\psi(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $\\mathbf F= P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ if \n\n$$\nP = \\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial y}, \\qquad Q = -\\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial y} = x^3-3xy^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial x} = -y^3+3x^2y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\psi(x,y) = x^3y - xy^3 + f(x), \\qquad \n\\psi(x,y) = -xy^3 + x^3y + g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\psi(x,y) = x^3y - xy^3.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curve of the stream function $\\psi(x,y) = x^3y - xy^3$ that passes through $P.$\nFirst, we find the value of the stream function at $P{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(-1,1) & =(-1)^{3}(1)-(-1)(1)^{3} \\\\  & =-1-(-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the streamline that passes through $P(-1,1)$ is the $0$-level curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}y-x{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ xy({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ xy(x+y)(x-y) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our possible streamlines are $x=0,$ $y=0,$ $y=-x,$ or $y=x.$ The streamline that passes through $P(-1,1)$ is $y=-x.$\nThe vector field and the streamline through the point $P$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/29/29512dff5cf2dfe6dbebc0fadeee51ee3043b0161dc1729cc89877e6b39512af.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179437 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/id #uuid "6cf11fc9-874f-5d59-bff0-1ed3debcbd40" :question/math-academy-id "e-12446" :question/problem "Find a stream function for the vector field $\\mathbf F,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = 2y\\,\\mathbf{i} +2x\\,\\mathbf{j}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $\\mathbf{F} = P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ with a simply connected domain $D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2$ has a stream function $\\psi(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} = 0.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) =  2y\\,\\mathbf{i} +2x\\,\\mathbf{j}$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D=\\mathbb{R}^2,$ where $P(x,y) = 2y$ and $Q(x,y) =2x.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\mathbf F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial x} + \\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} = 0 + 0 = 0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $\\psi(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $\\mathbf F= P\\,\\mathbf{i} + Q\\,\\mathbf{j}$ if \n\n$$\nP = \\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial y}, \\qquad Q = -\\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial y} = 2y, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial \\psi}{\\partial x} = -2x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\psi(x,y) = y^2 + f(x), \\qquad \n\\psi(x,y) = -x^2+ g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f(x)=-x^2$ and $g(y)=y^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\psi(x,y) = y^2-x^2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf214f38-9614-5b17-8467-b73171b563e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177868} {:answer/id #uuid "c071057e-cc88-5774-8550-f80dfae0ad85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = x^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177869} {:answer/id #uuid "c4136ff7-61e5-5824-b8d6-8bfdff8c5167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = xy^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177870} {:answer/id #uuid "4aa44a00-ba08-5a3b-9194-3746c23a21a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = 2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177871} {:answer/id #uuid "65323ed0-7186-569d-b96d-d952e703e09f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177872}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b1a0f0-52c7-552f-8f30-6e87f40ec522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177867}] :question/id #uuid "60134b61-53f9-50e7-85c6-4445150f503c" :question/math-academy-id "q-126829" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x, y) = x^{2}i - 2xyj$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "953fd242-8181-5605-91fe-317fa11da825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178180} {:answer/id #uuid "95cdb75d-7f04-586b-8f9f-3315263dbb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = y - xy^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178181} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d0a190-b264-5edd-a0ad-8628bba48d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) = 1 - xy^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178182} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca66a3b-e212-52f6-8a21-f55a0986e019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) =-4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178183} {:answer/id #uuid "298c2b69-931e-5a54-8ea4-e3bf4cabfb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x, y) =-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178184}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b2f1e142-6aa3-5c72-9320-64f30d6f7c91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178179}] :question/id #uuid "4bf80022-982e-52f6-a693-b1484ab92175" :question/math-academy-id "q-161437" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x, y) = (1 - 2xy)i - y^{2}j$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30cae81-5bda-52dc-8de4-9ad5fd587e48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Streamlines of Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a923c54f-6242-52ec-a161-8420bfdec595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178216} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc0d7ed-bc38-596b-b3f8-a34c5e14d6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x^{2}} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178217} {:answer/id #uuid "f52928a8-bdf5-5b6e-a372-9163511ebaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\frac{1}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178218} {:answer/id #uuid "01e3d527-be8f-5d0f-b866-2d47479c67bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178219} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8cc49f-2af4-520c-b024-00127b0c7dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{2}{x^{2}} - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178220}] :answer-field/id #uuid "237fbd10-d1da-5671-995b-e3827cd7ef2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eac7ad4-820f-5c18-9773-ebf398898a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372015} {:answer/id #uuid "282750a9-b937-50f2-972a-4e331bd8e692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372016} {:answer/id #uuid "373316d8-46cd-53f6-9b91-7cb17ade342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372017} {:answer/id #uuid "27a69ac4-2f12-5bf5-8488-d73f81f4be67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372018} {:answer/id #uuid "4883ebfa-3093-54d8-a60b-84cb2521bc67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "373316d8-46cd-53f6-9b91-7cb17ade342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372017} :answer-field/id #uuid "5729d00f-ef28-5624-a8a5-015c4a539268" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eca1e58e-6616-5dd0-8afa-579d4de9a32a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162209" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the streamline that passes through the point $P(-1,-1)$ for the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-2xy\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n. \n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-2xy\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={x}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=-2xy.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2x+(-2x)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}={x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=2xy.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={x}^{2}y+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}y+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={x}^{2}y.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curve of the stream function $ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}y$ that passes through $P.$\nFirst, we find the value of the stream function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(-1,-1) & =(-1)^{2}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the streamline that passes through $P(-1,-1)$ is the $-1$-level curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}y & =-1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the streamline that passes through $P(-1,-1)$ is $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$\nThe vector field and the streamline through the point $P$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b8/b803554d852d985c8feca61804a9e52423391fc4624a01c4199d0744fbf2e28d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7abceeb-620d-5e95-93ca-30bc557cf007" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Vector Field From Its Stream Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6596a7e1-33c8-5770-ad3d-4bd6746339f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(6{x}^{2}+3xy)\\,i-3{x}^{2}y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372036} {:answer/id #uuid "1019de8d-9796-54d8-a7d7-3867ddbc355e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-3{x}^{2}\\,i-(3{x}^{2}y+3x{y}^{2})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372037} {:answer/id #uuid "db8a7224-0ec3-5591-a0e7-169572aceb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+6xy\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372038} {:answer/id #uuid "98c5d095-62c9-5b47-a91b-d7f4bc4717c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(3{x}^{2}-3x{y}^{2})\\,i-3{x}^{2}y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372039} {:answer/id #uuid "af0a43c0-1af9-50b5-8508-84ab433607d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-6xy\\,i-(3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af0a43c0-1af9-50b5-8508-84ab433607d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-6xy\\,i-(3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372040} :answer-field/id #uuid "c25bb45f-532f-5ba4-9fd3-2f3c979bc106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65d2f94e-229a-51fd-a26e-3f0815f0eb18" :question/math-academy-id "q-162492" :question/problem "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $ψ(x,y)={x}^{3}-3x{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $ψ(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-3x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6xy, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-3x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $ψ(x,y)={x}^{3}-3x{y}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =-6xy\\,i-(3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7abceeb-620d-5e95-93ca-30bc557cf007" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Vector Field From Its Stream Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4c35f35-505d-5b86-9167-ceefb238af14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-x)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372043} {:answer/id #uuid "0b599044-693d-54d2-b820-f738cb7bb060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(-2x+1)\\,i+2y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372044} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b4cd56-a295-5ee8-bdb9-0604ff265037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(2y+x)\\,i+2x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372045} {:answer/id #uuid "2e5b38c9-5492-5744-91b2-bc509b4b6280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=(y+1)\\,i-{x}^{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372046} {:answer/id #uuid "1dea751c-2b96-5f6e-8cf0-07f9421b0d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=2y\\,i+(2x-1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dea751c-2b96-5f6e-8cf0-07f9421b0d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=2y\\,i+(2x-1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372047} :answer-field/id #uuid "57871c32-9592-5d5b-b52f-978468b21542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fea8348f-c35f-5297-af8d-bffb135e2427" :question/math-academy-id "q-162493" :question/problem "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+x.$" :question/worked-solution "A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $ψ(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2y, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =2y\\,i+(2x-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7abceeb-620d-5e95-93ca-30bc557cf007" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Vector Field From Its Stream Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de0e353-ab6e-59bc-a0ed-36c03e15387b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372050} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8be957-5e7a-5c11-9e63-50310cedd0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372051} {:answer/id #uuid "42f0507b-1475-5ce6-b8db-506235509208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372052} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa5c9a6-5913-5d25-b0d5-b24f5f1a2717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372053} {:answer/id #uuid "7729c754-88f0-530c-869b-5bdc5168a17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a8be957-5e7a-5c11-9e63-50310cedd0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372051} :answer-field/id #uuid "b231bed0-a79c-51f5-8734-2ba409222c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43559bcb-c65a-577f-8d0a-2160e10d1cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162494" :question/problem "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x.$" :question/worked-solution "A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $ψ(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7abceeb-620d-5e95-93ca-30bc557cf007" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Vector Field From Its Stream Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d5a9ef4-568a-5626-abf8-f9bb8294f9a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = ye^{xy}(2 + yx)i - (y^{3}e^{xy} + 2x)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178222} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b165a4-0d4d-55b3-b5eb-3897f111146b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = xe^{xy}(2 + y)i - (y^{2}e^{xy} + 2x)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178223} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2378e8-a76c-5838-8c4e-7ad80c206638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = xe^{xy}(2 + yx)i - (yxe^{xy} + 2x)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178224} {:answer/id #uuid "766b58cf-99c6-54dd-9b16-5ae500db93ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = yxe^{xy}(2 + yx)i - (y^{2}xe^{xy} + 2x)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178225} {:answer/id #uuid "79325398-1ef5-5639-aff5-a093511d2b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = ye^{xy}(2 + y)i - (y^{3}e^{xy} + 2x)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178226}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c322713a-088c-53bf-ac8d-8ce18e48102c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178221}] :question/id #uuid "2b583ac2-a10b-5624-9dd5-8092730bcd5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162514" :question/problem "Construct the vector field that has the stream function $ψ(x, y) = y^{2}e^{xy} + x^{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeb916fe-deac-5c6b-a3af-a1e29579a5af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372064} {:answer/id #uuid "ee658281-8425-5be1-8788-54102c3c6175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372065} {:answer/id #uuid "660c3c54-a204-504f-ae3d-31a70939bfb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372066} {:answer/id #uuid "160f71b3-9073-5c2f-99f9-acde1bf550a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372067} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0c4912-d2bd-5e3f-9221-2060507e5033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "160f71b3-9073-5c2f-99f9-acde1bf550a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372067} :answer-field/id #uuid "337543b8-07ff-5870-85da-be792a9109dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fb4a1a9-80b2-5c9b-b44c-5418f559f461" :question/math-academy-id "q-162518" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j?$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67b8f6d6-9607-5514-abbd-603cb08ece42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372078} {:answer/id #uuid "72008387-8f3a-5d1d-965c-282a4ef1a635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372079} {:answer/id #uuid "7b24f282-d62b-5e80-a78c-10312ff8606e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372080} {:answer/id #uuid "7a7e266d-e3fe-59e3-b2ef-457c0782331f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372081} {:answer/id #uuid "be1595e1-671d-5e1a-95b7-d83ff63e6f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)=-xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67b8f6d6-9607-5514-abbd-603cb08ece42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372078} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cada9ed-c85a-58fb-a254-1769ba4f3d5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "622f220e-fb66-51d7-b3ac-edc3a1b8924a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162520" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,j?$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ and $Q(x,y)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a no stream function, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=(1-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\ne 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffa79034-bdcc-5524-aa39-e81a79b48ded" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Stream Function for a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e32f2c3b-fa9c-5bf6-a35b-57839d0e21d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372085} {:answer/id #uuid "703dbab9-9c69-5646-a97b-dd8ef0a32c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}+2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372086} {:answer/id #uuid "b03ae81f-442d-5398-a1d0-eb48182ed670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372087} {:answer/id #uuid "06d4c7ba-315f-5ed3-b710-82a77b517287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}+xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372088} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb65d35-dc25-51cf-95b6-281265b1d418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}-4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e32f2c3b-fa9c-5bf6-a35b-57839d0e21d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ has no stream function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372085} :answer-field/id #uuid "126114a5-a04b-5b6e-a5e7-1561c7926bd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fa02a5c-65fb-5f22-a3ed-8e6c445f1c62" :question/math-academy-id "q-162522" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)=2xy\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j?$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=2xy\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a no stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2y+2y=4y\\ne 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc613be0-2d34-5253-8fbe-7d2a5fcd0840" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cases Where a Stream Function Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443cde18-cc2d-5bdd-84e4-9c0b1b2a779e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471137} {:answer/id #uuid "35df4025-24f4-5f6d-9b0e-90ee3d79b3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443cde18-cc2d-5bdd-84e4-9c0b1b2a779e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471137} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aefae05-b840-5479-a0a7-2de47e658a24" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895d98e1-fab9-5e72-a3d1-d971df11820d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471139} {:answer/id #uuid "61452935-e5e5-59b6-9d78-564209c02408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895d98e1-fab9-5e72-a3d1-d971df11820d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471139} :answer-field/id #uuid "6247ce83-8b63-5840-8ce5-806b28d78697" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7fdd654-374f-59e8-b8e4-99c8874f03fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471141} {:answer/id #uuid "dd875822-775d-5a88-bc58-dabb28f156b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd875822-775d-5a88-bc58-dabb28f156b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471142} :answer-field/id #uuid "421f632a-0626-55da-a2f8-ea9fdef58e6d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f67f3f6-b8ed-585a-bae8-a685dca4c830" :question/math-academy-id "q-162608" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=3x\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=x\\,i+x{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-2xy\\,j$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=3,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=3+(-2y)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=1+2xy\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2x+(-2x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc613be0-2d34-5253-8fbe-7d2a5fcd0840" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cases Where a Stream Function Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23fab97c-e1f7-53b4-896d-07255d63846f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471143} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4fc938-250e-53f2-85a0-98be5523667f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23fab97c-e1f7-53b4-896d-07255d63846f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471143} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ed52428-3dc5-589b-b8e0-fe9129bf90fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c0fe81d-9c21-54ac-a85d-9bebb1a995c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471145} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7a1df8-4146-5215-baf8-de5bbcdb3dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7a1df8-4146-5215-baf8-de5bbcdb3dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471146} :answer-field/id #uuid "91a453c2-3e96-5a19-838f-30317badd3dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45b0ce87-9a2b-5518-a603-a8a975bf0e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471147} {:answer/id #uuid "da145025-1406-500a-87e7-1acea0d69846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da145025-1406-500a-87e7-1acea0d69846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471148} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d299e6-840f-5825-99c7-07a873676f11" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "169dc9ad-6608-5ab8-8ec5-7973ca027bd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162611" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n- **I.** $F(x,y)=4{y}^{2}x\\,i-x{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- **II.** $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$\n- **III.** $F(x,y)=2yx\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=4{y}^{2}+(-2xy)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2y+(-2y)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30cae81-5bda-52dc-8de4-9ad5fd587e48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Streamlines of Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3041c7b2-ad5d-59e4-a35f-cdd3f5a8ded4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372183} {:answer/id #uuid "8e0bfc27-933c-52a6-a9da-b121d5422481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pi {e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372184} {:answer/id #uuid "4b692407-30c1-5d1f-ac8b-4238f37dea05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372185} {:answer/id #uuid "1dbbfc69-0b08-5509-a6ec-62eeb283eb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372186} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8466d6-4bb0-570a-a74f-a68de142e108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8466d6-4bb0-570a-a74f-a68de142e108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372187} :answer-field/id #uuid "1626cb5c-1d71-5bed-88ae-3afa894a0595" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd6e61d1-6465-500e-9577-5af9c54bc069" :question/math-academy-id "q-162619" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the streamline that passes through the point $P(0,\\pi )$ for the vector field $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n. \n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curve of the stream function $ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ that passes through $P.$\nFirst, we find the value of the stream function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(0,\\pi ) & ={e}^{(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the streamline that passes through $P(0,\\pi )$ is the $0$-level curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our possible streamlines are $y=k\\pi $ for any integer $k.$ The streamline that passes through $P(0,\\pi )$ is $y=\\pi .$\nThe vector field and the streamline through the point $P$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/bd/bd732367a876d2e6bba6bf96728ebcf8430176d2f480bff30a054cac5389b1f2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30cae81-5bda-52dc-8de4-9ad5fd587e48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Streamlines of Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc9bdb8d-ad2b-5d91-86ca-825ec11037fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a1ce9b96f0bca4ec14e7ce60e5cebd72efc4421acfd4a65ba55e9c8a7d1d352.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389341} {:answer/id #uuid "678a4e30-3832-553e-8ea1-b4ab930f1cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/0799c425e6b33f2be8f115d7d0de9e5607bdef9f094a02381fc5197839d80d75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389342} {:answer/id #uuid "6db4de8e-dbc7-51ee-8ae9-5b089f44fbf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95fee99b51dc07130717569fcb90ab5e210bf2cc64811f536dc493e9c3e1588e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389343} {:answer/id #uuid "92bd4bba-9b1d-550f-a3d8-850c5ca8fd4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3a/3a3ef451c7e25ff33fb1820d5b8c98e10038c4ee058f627d93acf72989b7b794.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389344} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc3c2dd-f56c-5123-bcfe-941b923629fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb7119466ac4f884fca55cfb3fc0b487703249050211ff922549a702a047bb39.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92bd4bba-9b1d-550f-a3d8-850c5ca8fd4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3a/3a3ef451c7e25ff33fb1820d5b8c98e10038c4ee058f627d93acf72989b7b794.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389344} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce55e1ed-b422-5201-909f-65fba9887b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b93df85-0b3c-5ded-8201-a97d95285f56" :question/math-academy-id "q-162629" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=2xi-2y\\,j$ over the domain $D={R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=2xi-2y\\,j\n$$\n\n is a vector field with simply connected domain $D,$ where $P(x,y)=2x$ and $Q(x,y)=-2y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2-2=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=2y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=2xy+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)=2xy+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)=2xy.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curves of the stream function $ψ(x,y)=2xy$ given by the equations $ψ(x,y)=c.$\n\nNotice that the range of $ψ(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2xy & =c \\\\ y & =\\frac{c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas with asymptotes $y=0$ and $x=0$ and, for $c=0,$ the lines $y=0$ and $x=0.$ Therefore, the correct graph (along with the vector field $F$) is as follows:\n\n![](images/24/24c6dadd4f980121a36929a9cdb800f7da8fac8eb84af40d595af89aa77b11ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30cae81-5bda-52dc-8de4-9ad5fd587e48" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Streamlines of Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9a4a14-a956-5391-ac3a-4943156bef2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/3296bdd0ae6e92949ee3728e01592f1758917cf03446e75317af341ef669f606.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389348} {:answer/id #uuid "abbaeebd-0469-5172-b7c3-8cb76cac7c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9ba45e905fc98c5011727c483ba444088c81a0423cc85912af24e1e8c19f1cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389349} {:answer/id #uuid "e67f9b71-0c0d-5761-ba3f-d60318d3579b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/75/7585305cff504d86c4b910455acb21036503bdc0073989ca8351a751f1fea9b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389350} {:answer/id #uuid "a8aac5dd-ff50-5af5-a307-0a9ee9b5c0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff6709c054d8c1e3cd21bbe87e7326f802471fa321a90346e3f173f72b443896.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389351} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff7114c-d67e-5f98-a63a-d5f5e37f4d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6926d3f6d26fe712b53e53c06af440575dbe858e373cfae5d7d4b5017f44b93.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abbaeebd-0469-5172-b7c3-8cb76cac7c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9ba45e905fc98c5011727c483ba444088c81a0423cc85912af24e1e8c19f1cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389349} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9db8e2f-b628-5684-b658-6125f7acf877" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc28542a-a43a-5f01-b243-0063900eefa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-162630" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the streamlines of the vector field $F(x,y)=2y\\,i+2x\\,j$ over the domain $D={R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=2y\\,i+2x\\,j\n$$\n\n is a vector field with simply connected domain $D,$ where $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=-2x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={y}^{2}+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)=-{x}^{2}+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f(x)=-{x}^{2}$ or $g(y)={y}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curves of the stream function $ψ(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}$ given by the equations $ψ(x,y)=c.$\n\nNotice that the range of $ψ(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas with asymptotes $y=x$ and $x=-x$ and, for $c=0,$ the lines $y=x$ and $y=-x.$ Therefore, the correct graph (along with the vector field $F$) is as follows:\n\n![](images/9b/9b0d2f98a0b71beb773b802908f01691924492a5f3abff3db75be4a0ae458e7d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc613be0-2d34-5253-8fbe-7d2a5fcd0840" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Cases Where a Stream Function Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8719c4c1-296a-5308-8304-35f3d974ce70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178228} {:answer/id #uuid "90a5767b-02fa-5b05-a4c9-973f6b09f516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178229} {:answer/id #uuid "996baf61-e5f6-5df1-aa32-1851db148914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178230} {:answer/id #uuid "ff342f1d-0cbd-5406-9161-19ff3ff1afe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178231} {:answer/id #uuid "7776b280-63fe-5dc8-85a0-f54e021ddc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178232}] :answer-field/id #uuid "712e9e01-c44e-5384-90fb-ae7811625631" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178227}] :question/id #uuid "58115dca-1aaa-5449-a87f-7951d165abcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-162640" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\n1. $F(x, y) = 4xyi + y^{4}j$\n2. $F(x, y) = \\cos (3x)i + 3y\\sin (3x)j$\n3. $F(x, y) = e^{xy}i - ye^{x}j$"}]}
